# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The house style, written down.
#
# Derived from what the tree already looked like rather than chosen: the
# knobs below are the ones that make clang-format agree with the existing
# code, and each was set by measuring the diff against files nobody had
# touched. It is not a redesign -- it is the smallest description of what
# was already being typed by hand.
#
# **ReflowComments is off, and that is the important line.** The comments
# in this tree are its main asset; several of them are the only record of
# a defect that cost a session to find. Letting a formatter rewrap them
# would churn exactly the text worth preserving and make every future
# `git blame` on a comment point here. Checked: comment *text* is
# byte-identical across the whole tree after formatting.
#
# The two alignment options are off for the same reason -- the tree
# aligns assignments in some places and not others, deliberately, and
# forcing either answer everywhere is a large diff that says nothing.

BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 80
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
PointerAlignment: Right
AlignConsecutiveAssignments: false
AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: false
AlignTrailingComments: false
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: false
ReflowComments: false

# Include order is meaningful here: a platform's own header first, then
# the shared runner, then emucore, then the system. Sorting would put
# <errno.h> above "board.h" and lose that.
SortIncludes: false
